# Brand Rules (NON-NEGOTIABLE)

The site is a **Next.js** (App Router, TypeScript, plain CSS Modules) port of the **Claude** version. Its look must never change except by explicit user request.

## Rule 1: The Claude brand always governs
- Every page, section, and element in this project MUST follow the Claude brand rules. No exceptions.
- Source of truth, in order: `public/host-keira.css` (canonical tokens), `public/brand-guide.html`, then existing components in `components/`.
- `app/globals.css` mirrors the `public/host-keira.css` tokens. Keep both in sync.
- Use the `--hk-*` variables. Do not hardcode new colors, fonts, or sizes.
- Do not introduce a new visual style, palette, font, or component pattern.

## Rule 2: Astra content must be adapted to the Claude brand
- Sections and elements may be borrowed from the Astra version, but only their structure, content, and behavior.
- Restyle everything borrowed with Claude tokens before it reaches the site.
- Never bring in Astra's `brand.css`, `styles.css`, `brand-guide.css`, or `BRAND-GUIDE.md`.
- If an Astra element cannot be expressed in the Claude brand, stop and ask the user.
- The old `astra/` and `claude/` folders were deleted. Originals are in git commit `03f53f1` (`git show 03f53f1:astra/dist/index.html`).

## Claude brand quick reference
- Fonts: Playfair Display (headings), Montserrat (body, labels), Great Vibes (script accents). Loaded with `next/font` in `app/layout.tsx`. NOT Astra's Cormorant Garamond.
- Colors: gold `#D4AF37`, black `#0B0A09`, beige `#F5EBD7`, ivory `#FBF6EC`, text `#141210`, dark gold text `#8A6D1F`.
- Square corners (radius 0). Only exception: the floating Messenger pill.
- Sections alternate dark and light backgrounds.
- Section header: uppercase eyebrow, then a Playfair H2.

## Code conventions
- One component per file in `components/`, with a matching `.module.css`. Shared pieces live in `components/ui.module.css`.
- Page copy and link constants live in `lib/content.ts`.
- Server components by default. Add `"use client"` only for state or browser APIs.
- Layout switching uses CSS media queries, not JavaScript window-width checks.

## Conflicts
- If an instruction conflicts with these rules, state the conflict and ask the user before proceeding.
